{'_client': <twikit.client.client.Client object at 0x000001E534E2AE40>, '_data': {'__typename': 'Tweet', 'rest_id': '1877700886379823319', 'core': {'user_results': {'result': {'__typename': 'User', 'id': 'VXNlcjoxMTAxMjAyOTE1MjE2MjQ4ODMy', 'rest_id': '1101202915216248832', 'affiliates_highlighted_label': {}, 'has_graduated_access': True, 'is_blue_verified': True, 'profile_image_shape': 'Circle', 'legacy': {'can_dm': False, 'can_media_tag': True, 'created_at': 'Thu Feb 28 19:30:09 +0000 2019', 'default_profile': True, 'default_profile_image': False, 'description': '', 'entities': {'description': {'urls': []}}, 'fast_followers_count': 0, 'favourites_count': 20481, 'followers_count': 303, 'friends_count': 1214, 'has_custom_timelines': True, 'is_translator': False, 'listed_count': 5, 'location': '', 'media_count': 832, 'name': 'Kiddocious', 'normal_followers_count': 303, 'pinned_tweet_ids_str': [], 'possibly_sensitive': False, 'profile_image_url_https': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1776386528039567360/aLglry5N_normal.jpg', 'profile_interstitial_type': '', 'screen_name': 'Kiddocious1', 'statuses_count': 7558, 'translator_type': 'none', 'verified': False, 'want_retweets': False, 'withheld_in_countries': []}}}}, 'unmention_data': {}, 'edit_control': {'edit_tweet_ids': ['1877700886379823319'], 'editable_until_msecs': '1736517351000', 'is_edit_eligible': False, 'edits_remaining': '5'}, 'is_translatable': False, 'views': {'count': '7', 'state': 'EnabledWithCount'}, 'source': '<a href="http://twitter.com/download/android" rel="nofollow">Twitter for Android</a>', 'note_tweet': {'is_expandable': True, 'note_tweet_results': {'result': {'id': 'Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjE4Nzc3MDA4ODYwODYyMDEzNDQ=', 'text': '@TheChiefNerd \nEven though I know you\'re a 🤡 ...I hope this helps...\n\nScenario:\n\nIn the midst of a global health crisis, a government mandates that to participate in basic societal functions, individuals must either:\n\nOption A: Get vaccinated with a new, experimental vaccine that has limited long-term safety data. This vaccine is touted as the only way to curb the spread of the disease, but there are concerns about side effects, long-term impacts, and the speed at which it was developed.\nOption B: Refuse the vaccine and be subjected to significant restrictions on your freedoms. This includes:\nLoss of Employment: Workplaces require vaccination proof, meaning you could lose your job or be unable to work.\nShopping Restrictions: Many stores, grocery shops included, only allow entry to vaccinated individuals, severely limiting where you can buy essentials.\nTravel Limitations: Public and even some private transport systems require vaccination status for use, essentially grounding you unless you travel by foot or own a vehicle, which might not be feasible for everyone.\nSocial Isolation: Social venues like restaurants, gyms, or entertainment centers are off-limits without proof of vaccination, leading to a form of social ostracism.\n\nThe Ridiculous Argument:\n\nAfter choosing to get vaccinated because your livelihood and basic functionality in society depend on it, someone might argue, "You chose this; no one forced you to get vaccinated. You could have chosen not to get it."\n\nWhy This Argument Is Flawed:\n\nCoercion by Necessity: The "choice" here is between a medical procedure with uncertain long-term effects or losing your ability to engage in society\'s basic functions. This isn\'t a choice in the traditional sense but a coercion where one\'s basic rights and needs are leveraged to force compliance.\nFalse Binary: Presenting this as a choice implies there\'s an equitable or reasonable alternative when, in fact, both options carry significant personal and societal costs. Not getting vaccinated doesn\'t free you from the situation; it binds you to a life of severe restriction.\nLack of True Consent: Informed consent for medical procedures generally requires understanding all risks and benefits, with the option to opt-out without repercussions. Here, the repercussions (loss of livelihood, freedom) make the consent under duress, not freely given.\nMoral and Ethical Pressure: The choice isn\'t just about personal health but about survival in society, making it laden with ethical dilemmas, especially when one\'s decision impacts their ability to provide for themselves or their family.\nSystemic Pressure: The argument ignores the systemic pressures and societal structures that create these binary conditions, essentially blaming individuals for navigating a system designed to leave them with no good options.\n\nThis situation illustrates how "you chose this" can be an oversimplification or a form of victim-blaming, ignoring the coercive nature of the choices presented and the societal structures that enforce them. It\'s not about individual choice but about the lack of real, equitable options in the face of systemic enforcement.', 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}]}, 'richtext': {'richtext_tags': []}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Fri Jan 10 12:55:51 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1877347490887811322', 'display_text_range': [14, 289], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}, {'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [14, 27]}]}, 'favorite_count': 0, 'favorited': False, 'full_text': "@TheChiefNerd @TheChiefNerd \nEven though I know you're a 🤡 ...I hope this helps...\n\nScenario:\n\nIn the midst of a global health crisis, a government mandates that to participate in basic societal functions, individuals must either:\n\nOption A: Get vaccinated with a new, experimental vaccine", 'in_reply_to_screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'in_reply_